      "cve": "CVE-2026-114437",
      "ids": [
        {
          "system_name": "SUSE CVE Page",
          "text": "https://www.suse.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-114437"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        {
          "category": "general",
          "text": "In the Golang Chi web framework, the ClientIPFromXFF middleware skips any X-Forwarded-For entry in a configured trusted CIDR but never verifies that the direct TCP peer in http.Request.RemoteAddr belongs to that CIDR. A client that can reach the Go server directly can therefore append a trusted-looking proxy address and choose the client IP returned by middleware.GetClientIP.\n\nThis issue affects chi before 5.4.0.",
          "title": "CVE description"
        }
      ],
